{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1003594-2e-how-to-seduce-mortal","id":1003594,"title":"[2E] How to seduce mortal?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-15T14:09:57-08:00","id":1003594,"title":"[2E] How to seduce mortal?","content":"In <b>Dresden Files</b> universe, vampires makes specific toxin that is extremely pleasant to victim. In <b>Vampire: The Masquared - Bloodlines</b> game I remember that vampire Kiss was overtly pleasure ( almost orgasmic ) to mortal. Is it still working this way in Requiem 2E?<br /> <br /> <b>Another question is how can vampire make other mortal or supernatural being to have pleasant thought about him?</b> Does something like getting Kindred blood to moral can make them under spell of vampire?<br /> <br /> I do not write here about full Blood Bond - rather that putting few Bloods drops would work like narcotic on the mortal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T14:21:45-08:00","id":1003604,"title":"","content":"You should probably read the book for this, but yes the blood bond is the primary way to go.<br /> <br /> Just feeding off of someone, nicely not in a violent way, gives them the Swooning Condition towards you. This makes them attracted to you and vulnerable to your advances.<br /> <br /> You mentioned the full Blood Bond, but you don't have to instantly go to that. There's three stages, with the third being the full Vinculum. All three stages offer great bonuses to using Disciplines against the thrall and making them more susceptible to Social actions, as well as making harming the vampire a Breaking Point roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T14:52:56-08:00","id":1003619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1003594-2e-how-to-seduce-mortal#post1003594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In <b>Dresden Files</b> universe, vampires makes specific toxin that is extremely pleasant to victim. In <b>Vampire: The Masquared - Bloodlines</b> game I remember that vampire Kiss was overtly pleasure ( almost orgasmic ) to mortal. Is it still working this way in Requiem 2E?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it is. Page 56:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The vampire is well adapted to feeding. When he is ready, his fangs descend. Exposure to the traces of vampire blood in his mouth, as well as the bite itself, create a feeling of intense euphoria in the recipient. Vampires call this the Kiss. This is love and lust for both parties. This is the sex you know you should not have, but will come back for. </div> </div> </div>And, on page 95:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When feeding non-violently, the vampire\u2019s fangs cause an enticing, invigorating sensation that distracts the victim, to draw attention away from the reality of the feeding. Many Kindred use this method as part of a seduction. A mortal bitten subtly gains the Swooning Condition. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1003594-2e-how-to-seduce-mortal#post1003594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Another question is how can vampire make other mortal or supernatural being to have pleasant thought about him?</b> Does something like getting Kindred blood to moral can make them under spell of vampire?<br /> <br /> I do not write here about full Blood Bond - rather that putting few Bloods drops would work like narcotic on the mortal?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the Blood Bond comes in three stages, all of which endear the subject to the vampire to a gradually increasing degree. Even aside from blood bonds though, Vitae is powerfully addictive. Page 99:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Vitae is life. Life tastes very, very good. In fact, it tastes so good, it\u2019s highly addictive to both mortal and Kindred alike. Vitae\u2019s addictive quality is one of the strongest tools Kindred can bring to bear. Even ignoring the blood bond, Vitae is a remarkable bargaining chip. Just as in the mortal world, addiction\u2019s a terrible thing when leveraged against a person.<br /> Vitae addiction feels very similar to addiction to a strong drug. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T15:10:13-08:00","id":1003629,"title":"","content":"Three words: the Seductive Beast.<br /> <br /> By lashing out at a mortal with this facet of the Beast you automatically give them the Wanton Condition. This basically turns their inhibitions completely off, so seduction becomes effortless after that. And Majesty or the Kiss can easily take care of people not specifically attracted to your character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T03:25:27-08:00","id":1003842,"title":"","content":"And whar about other supernaturals? Would mage be simply Wooo by vampires Kiss or blood? If yes, would they resist with their Gnosis, for example?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T03:58:22-08:00","id":1003851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1003594-2e-how-to-seduce-mortal?p=1003842#post1003842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And whar about other supernaturals? Would mage be simply Wooo by vampires Kiss or blood? If yes, would they resist with their Gnosis, for example?</div> </div> </div> </div>Without any Mind protection yes. <br /> <br /> Normally vampires need to spend a willpower to effect supernaturals. But they say Warlocks &quot;Mages&quot; are affected normally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T05:20:47-08:00","id":1003872,"title":"","content":"P95, 'In reference to the effects of a bite, the word 'mortal' applies to humans, ghouls, warlocks, and other things that are mostly human. Vampires, werewolves, mummies, fairies and other thigns far removed from humanity are not normally subject to the Assault and the Kiss. The bite is pleasurable or unsettling, just not mechanically so.'<br /> <br /> When drinking Vitae, two things happen. The first is you roll to see if you resist Vitae addiction with a Resolve + Composure, -1 for each point consumed. Otherwise one gets the Persistent Addicted Condition. This is the roll I believe you would use supernatural tolerance on. When dealing with the blood bond, p100 says, 'Kindred characters can attempt to resist the bond by spending Willpower. Make a Blood Potency roll, minus the number of Vitae ingested. The Willpower point does not add to this roll. If successful, that drink does not add to the bond. However, the character suffers Vitae addiction normally. Any further attempts to resist the bond from the same vampire suffer a cumulative -1 die penalty; even ancient Kindred cannot resist the bond forever. Mortals have no such defense.'<br /> <br /> I don't believe your supernatural tolerance would help in this, without some house rules. As Rose Bailey has said, '<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/151667-nwod-mages-and-vampires?p=151934#post151934\">The blood bond works on mages (or anyone else) the same as on normal humans.</a>'<br /> <br /> Though yes, Mind protection could work to defend against it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T07:29:21-08:00","id":1003929,"title":"","content":"Seductive Beast, blood bonds (enhanced via Honey Trap and Voivoid), the Kiss, the Daeva-signature Kiss of the Succubus merit and Majesty discipline, Auspex for knowing best way to act or Auspex 4 to inflict a Condition. I'm sure there are other creative options out there using other abilities.<br /> <br /> On the mundane side, we have the Inspiring Merit, the Pusher and Sympathetic merits, rolling an exceptional success on a social roll (hello social Styles and Prof Training), things like Barfly / Fame / Striking Looks / Taste to fit in.<br /> <br /> Mages are actually a bit more vulnerable than other supernaturals, given that they are still human, unless an appropriate Shielding spell is in place. No Gnosis to resist the Kiss. Its also arguable what kind of Shielding will protect against against the Kiss or the Predator's aura, given the details of those two (drug-like reaction in the body, needing Life? Mind for a mental issue? Death, since its an undead?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 11-16-2016, 10:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T07:52:14-08:00","id":1003936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1003594-2e-how-to-seduce-mortal?p=1003629#post1003629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Three words: the Seductive Beast.<br /> <br /> By lashing out at a mortal with this facet of the Beast you automatically give them the Wanton Condition. This basically turns their inhibitions completely off, so seduction becomes effortless after that. And Majesty or the Kiss can easily take care of people not specifically attracted to your character.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, you don't automatically inflict the Wanton Condition. Even plain vanilla humans are capable of lashing back to avoid it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T08:15:38-08:00","id":1003945,"title":"","content":"They can't lash back; they don't have a Beast and they don't inflict a Condition if they win. They can resist, though.<br /> <br /> I also wouldn't allow Supernatural Tolerance to help resist Vitae Addiction, given even Vampires don't get to add Blood Potency to that roll.<br /> <br /> But yeah, social manipulation is kind of the specialty of the Vampire splat. If you want to manipulate mortals, via seduction or any other means, Vampires have you covered quite thoroughly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T08:15:54-08:00","id":1003946,"title":"","content":"Remember that Mages can use Pattern Restoration to remove any Mental Condition affecting them. So if your Mage doesn't like what he feels, he can press &quot;spend mana to be free&quot; button to purge it.<br /> <br /> Obvious problem here is the question if they really want to remove that wonderful feeling.<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> Basically, Mage is vulnerable ass hell to being inflicted with vampiric means of control, but they have by far easiest time removing them. Main &quot;thing&quot; is making sure your Mage KNOWS that they should pattern purge these things away, even if they are super duper pleasant. Basically, a Wisemans trial.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 11-16-2016, 11:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T08:20:28-08:00","id":1003950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1003594-2e-how-to-seduce-mortal?p=1003872#post1003872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When drinking Vitae ... you roll to see if you resist Vitae addiction with a Resolve + Composure, -1 for each point consumed. Otherwise one gets the Persistent Addicted Condition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quick clarification question: is this -1 per point consumed done:<br /> <br /> A. <b>Per the instance of feeding vitae.</b> In other words if fed 2 points tonight it is at -2. If fed 1 vitae tomorrow night that will be a separate roll at -1 (and yes, a total of 2 steps toward blood bond).<br /> <br /> B. <b>Cumulative per the character.</b> In other words if fed 2 points tonight for the first time it is at -2. If fed 1 vitae tomorrow night that will be a separate roll, again, at -3 (cumulative points drunk).<br /> <br /> If A, then a high Resolve + Composure can permit promiscuous social vitae drinking without becoming addicted, so long as you're lucky with dice.<br /> <br /> If B, then you really need to avoid all vitae if you want to never get addicted.<br /> <br /> I'd just like to better understand the intent of the setting in the expression of mechanics. <br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T09:17:47-08:00","id":1003978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1003594-2e-how-to-seduce-mortal?p=1003950#post1003950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quick clarification question: is this -1 per point consumed done:<br /> <br /> A. <b>Per the instance of feeding vitae.</b> In other words if fed 2 points tonight it is at -2. If fed 1 vitae tomorrow night that will be a separate roll at -1 (and yes, a total of 2 steps toward blood bond).</div> </div> </div> </div>This one.<br /> <br /> Yes, it's possible to resist the addiction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T09:46:47-08:00","id":1003990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1003594-2e-how-to-seduce-mortal?p=1003945#post1003945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They can't lash back; they don't have a Beast and they don't inflict a Condition if they win. They can resist, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>My book says they can lash back, they just don't inflict a condition. It doesn't say one way or the other if they win they get or don't get the +2 bonus to pursuing the Beast's aspect, if they retaliate. (Probably not but if the mortal is or once was a ghoul, or a psychic with empathic sensitivities who knows.) It also says mortals get a +2 to fight, flee, or neutralize the threat represented by the predatory aura they are confronted with. So yes they can lash back, and no, inflicting the Wanton Condition on someone is not automatic just by using the predatory aura on someone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T10:02:13-08:00","id":1003996,"title":"","content":"Resisting a Lashing Out is not actually called Lashing Out, but it uses the same mechanics. Saying that a mortal lashes back or resists means the same thing. Mortals just aren't literally lashing back the way vampires does since they don't have a Beast to Lash Out with.<br /> I believe the +2 bonus for attacking, fleeing or neutralizing the aggressor is meant to replace the vampire's +2 for pursuing their chosen aspect's interests since mortals don't have a beast with independent interests.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T11:59:44-08:00","id":1004042,"title":"","content":"A good Manipulation + Subterfuge roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/822-daemonchrno","name":"DaemonChrno","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar822_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T12:19:35-08:00","id":1004054,"title":"","content":"Have any of you considered, like, saying hello? Maybe throw out a compliment here and there. Some small talk. Ask questions about the other. Gradually increasing physical contact?<br /> <br /> By that I mean mundane social rolls. Understand tgat a feeding roll gets you one or more mortals under your sway ebough to be fed on with an hour's worth of work. That's pretty good. Blood bonds tebd to create more obsession than useful love, if done without reinforcing the relationship you want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T13:06:24-08:00","id":1004075,"title":"","content":"Wyrd seemed to specifically be asking about supernatural abilities, so that was how I answered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T13:43:13-08:00","id":1004100,"title":"","content":"Eh. Ive just been in a sarcastic mood lately. Sorry for being kind of douchy. <br /> <br /> I would argue that being able to seduce a mortal in a single roll enough to deliver The Kiss probably represents above average acumen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T07:10:44-08:00","id":1004390,"title":"","content":"Thanks for clarifying, Nofather.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1003594-2e-how-to-seduce-mortal?p=1003996#post1003996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Resisting a Lashing Out is not actually called Lashing Out, but it uses the same mechanics. Saying that a mortal lashes back or resists means the same thing. Mortals just aren't literally lashing back the way vampires does since they don't have a Beast to Lash Out with.<br /> I believe the +2 bonus for attacking, fleeing or neutralizing the aggressor is meant to replace the vampire's +2 for pursuing their chosen aspect's interests since mortals don't have a beast with independent interests.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps all mortals have their spiritual &quot;chi&quot; that flares in the presence of challenge? Flares and fails before the stronger beast, in most cases. But at the very least they are not complete putty in the hands of every newborn vamp. Or, well, an experienced mortal (hunter?) with decent stats isn't.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}